66c973e8 (797 1793285340417 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f347") (src . "store: a failed commit says why\n\ncommit-then guarded session-commit! with a catch-all that answered every\ncondition as (error unknown (commit-barrier-failed)), with no reason, no\nerrno and no log line, so a busy machine lock, a failed fsync and an\ninternal error read the same. A classifier, commit-failure, now names\nthe condition: a filesystem failure with its op, path, reason and errno;\na raised refusal as raised, for example (error store-busy (path ...));\na log error with its clauses; anything else as (failed internal (reason\n...)). The answer keeps its head and appends the (failed ...) clause, and\nthe event is traced as commit-failed. with-store-write's fallback, which\ndropped the failure of its own commit, now appends the same two clauses;\nit is reached when that second commit meets what the first did not, such\nas a lock busy now and free before. describe-log-error moves beside the\nclassifier in store.sc; rpc.sc still exports it.\n\n- answers.sc: exports failure-kind and failure-clauses.\n- store.sc: commit-failure; both commit sites; the fallback's comment.\n- rpc.sc: describe-log-error now comes from store.sc.\n- Tests: store1 (an fsync failure, a busy machine lock at the commit,\n  the classifier on each class and on objects of no class); q10 (the\n  fallback's commit refused); unreadable-census; rows-baseline.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 519))))
